      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe, so I need you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the usual maximum:\n\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Typical single dose:** 500 to 1,000 mg, and up to 850 mg three times daily with meals.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
